     It isn't based on the letters you usually see when examining
your inventory; it's based on the actual internal ordering of
objects.  They generally won't match except by coincidence (or
possibly after a save/restore cycle, but I don't think so).  To
see the real ordering, you should turn the `fixinv' option off so
that the letters get reassigned (consecutive a,b,&c on up) every
time you access inventory.  

     You should have seen anomalous behavior for *some* inventory
object, not necessarily the one you tried to target.  And if the
loadstones happen to be the very last item in the internal order,
you can expect nethack to crash.


